# Valgrind suppressions for luaext's best-effort CI leg
# (.github/workflows/ci.yml, job "best-effort" / "valgrind").
#
# Empty for now — there's no extension code to have known-safe findings
# against yet. As real false positives are identified (e.g. from PHP's own
# persistent allocations, OS-level one-time initialization, or intentional
# leaks in Zend startup) add suppressions here with a comment explaining
# WHY the leak is expected/safe, not just what it is. Never add a
# suppression to make a genuine leak in luaext's own code disappear.
#
# Format reference: https://valgrind.org/docs/manual/manual-core.html#manual-core.suppress
#
# Example shape (commented out — nothing suppressed yet):
#
# {
#   example_suppression_name
#   Memcheck:Leak
#   match-leak-kinds: reachable
#   ...
#   fun:example_function_name
# }
